# GD-24 (round 19, writer 10): settled; was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.4. L §2.4: a row read `after m` sorts "after the dated ones of its target and keys".
# The old comment:
# L §2.4 sorts version items "then by the start of their own governs span or their instant"; a reading `after m` (L
# §4.6: "just after movement m") has its place in time only on m's day, which the text doesn't hold (m's day is a
# value), so its order against `at D end` of one target and keys is not stated: REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED (it decides the
# canonical text, so the hash).
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..

version r
  cite s
  known 2026-03-02
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 5.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 end "wyciąg"
  stated[konto] = 3.00 PLN after pay[2026-03] "wyciąg"
